WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.539
- [Narrator] In two German
cities lies the birthplace

00:00:02.539 --> 00:00:05.240
of a worldwide arts revolution.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.619
One which looked to strip
buildings from unnecessary

00:00:07.619 --> 00:00:11.010
adornments and build the
foundation of what is called

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.130
modern architecture.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.983
Welcome to the home of Bauhaus.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.640
It all started here,
Weimar University, 1919.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.690
This is where German
architect, Walter Gropius,

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:30.330
alongside other artists,
founded the Bauhaus movement.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.940
His office alludes to what
the architectural style

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.617
would become-a force for
clean, simple designs

00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:38.090
fit for the everyday life.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:41.150
Not too far away in Weimar
is the first official

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.650
Bauhaus building, Haus am Horn,

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.760
built for an exhibition in 1923.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.160
Its clean lines and lack
of adornments might look

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.310
average today, but, almost
one hundred years ago,

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.670
it was truly revolutionary.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:58.980
Seventy miles away in Dessau,
the movement continued in 1925-

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.530
initiating its most fruitful period.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.810
The most stunning representation
is the Bauhaus Dessau.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:08.120
Seen as the pivotal building
in Bauhaus, this structure

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.640
amazed the world with its
steel frame construction

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.910
and asymmetrical plan.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:16.490
Nearby, you also have other
buildings in the Bauhaus style.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.740
The industrialist minimalist aesthetic

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.777
is visible in all of them.

00:01:20.777 --> 00:01:24.360
In 1932, the Bauhaus
school moved to Berlin,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.480
where it dissolved itself a year later,

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.720
due to the Nazi regime.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.490
Nevertheless, the movement
spread all around the world,

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:33.370
creating an international trend

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.520
for all other spheres of art.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.770
(electronic pop music)

